The situation wasn't as catastrophic as the events of 2013, yet it was undeniably alarming, with television screens broadcasting images of a raging river demolishing numerous buildings. Memories of 2013 flooded the mind, when torrential rains unleashed devastating flash floods from Kedarnath to Rishikesh, causing thousands of villages to endure hardship and resulting in over 5,000 individuals reported missing. Significant events such as the 2021 glacial lake outburst flood that ravaged Chamoli and the 2023 subsidence in Joshimath also stand out prominently.

