"Tropical cyclones have seen an increase in frequency over the last decade, typically occurring from November until March or April of the subsequent year," stated Dwikorita Karnawati, Chairwoman of BMKG, highlighting that Indonesia's broad swathes of susceptible regions, especially its elevated terrains and mountainous areas, are typically the first to experience the impacts of hydrometeorological disasters. She attributed the rising occurrence of cyclones to climate change.

