A new low-pressure system is anticipated to emerge in the Bay of Bengal approximately on September 20. “There is a chance of wind gusts developing, though a cyclone is improbable for now,” Mohapatra commented. The forecast is expected to provide more clarity in the days ahead, noting that the trajectory and strength of the system are contingent upon evolving meteorological conditions. He assured that there is no imminent threat of cyclones or severe weather conditions. The earlier low-pressure system, which caused heavy rainfall in the coastal and western districts, has diminished overall rainfall, though localized heavy showers and thunderstorms remain a threat, especially in regions susceptible to flooding and low-lying zones.
